ghpull:735 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "rdf_canon: bump oxrdf 0.2->0.3.3, boundary-convert for rdf-canon-upstream" ;
    bl:number 735 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:733 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr735 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:733 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-10-30T15:25:57Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-30T15:25:57Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr735Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #733 arose because dependabot PR #649's oxrdf 0.2.4->0.3.3 bump broke rdf_canon with a Dataset type mismatch: rdf_canon's own Cargo.toml still pinned oxrdf 0.2 while the rest of the workspace (via turtle) had moved to 0.3.3, and rdf_canon's canonicalize_dataset/canonicalize_graph pass a self-built oxrdf::Dataset straight into rdf-canon-upstream's canonicalize(), which is hard-pinned to oxrdf 0.2.4 with no 0.3-compatible release. PR #133 (this crate's original author) had explicitly reasoned the two oxrdf versions could coexist without conflict since nothing crossed between them -- true until #649 exposed the actual crossing point. Picked up a prior agent's partial fix (already in the worktree, interrupted mid-session): bump rdf_canon's own oxrdf to 0.3.3 matching turtle, keep a second aliased oxrdf02=0.2.4 dependency solely for rdf-canon-upstream's API, and add boundary-conversion functions (graph_name_to_v02/subject_to_v02/term_to_v02/literal_to_v02/dataset_to_v02) used only at the two canonicalize() call sites." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:735 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr735 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr735Decision .

session:pr735Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Kept rdf_canon's own Dataset/Quad/Term/Literal/GraphName construction on oxrdf 0.3.3 throughout, converting to 0.2.4 only at the narrow canonicalize() boundary, rather than reverting rdf_canon's whole internal representation back to 0.2.4 to match rdf-canon-upstream." ;
    agp:alternative "Downgrading rdf_canon's own oxrdf usage back to 0.2.4 (matching rdf-canon-upstream exactly, avoiding any conversion layer) was rejected: it would re-diverge rdf_canon from the rest of the workspace's oxrdf 0.3.3 (turtle, sparql_endpoint, etc.), recreating the exact two-versions-in-the-graph situation #649 exposed, just shifted to a different pair of call sites. A one-way conversion at the single external-crate boundary is more isolated and keeps rdf_canon's own code aligned with the workspace." .
